Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Align the Message Upgrade framework's authority check with the fix in SendRequest by performing a case-sensitive match against "mms" and "sms".

Previously, MessageUpgradeWorker classified the message type case-insensitively using toLowerCase(), causing it to attempt to upgrade case-variant URIs like "MMS". By matching case-sensitively, we immediately reject upgrades for unauthorized case-variant authorities, bypassing the upgrade bind flow and preventing potential service hangs.

Bug: 517377188
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
Test: atest MmsServiceRoboTests:com.android.mms.service.MmsRequestRoboTest
Ignore-AOSP-First: security

(cherry picked from commit 79de22baeaabe3755b2ed7f53dbfe279af5072b1)

Change-Id: Ic09ebb5565d8ddbeacdf5422d77ce2fffae4aff9

(cherry picked from commit d133c0ace50404096021dac5c2c1a5cfced03825)
---
 telephony/java/android/telephony/MessageUpgradeWorker.java | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/telephony/java/android/telephony/MessageUpgradeWorker.java b/telephony/java/android/telephony/MessageUpgradeWorker.java
index 059ce72b2..11f23fc4a 100644
--- a/telephony/java/android/telephony/MessageUpgradeWorker.java
+++ b/telephony/java/android/telephony/MessageUpgradeWorker.java
@@ -582,7 +582,7 @@ public class MessageUpgradeWorker {
             return MessageType.UNKNOWN;
         }
 
-        return switch (contentUri.getAuthority().toLowerCase()) {
+        return switch (contentUri.getAuthority()) {
             case AUTHORITY_SMS -> MessageType.SMS;
             case AUTHORITY_MMS -> MessageType.MMS;
             default -> MessageType.UNKNOWN;
